			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Inject cross-frame postMessage and SkyBridge diagnostics\n\nExtend the `RuntimeDiagnostics` transform plugin to capture cross-frame communication telemetry and specific `SkyBridge` lifecycle events within extension webviews.\n\nThe injected runtime code now includes:\n1. A `message` event listener that logs `postMessage` traffic between the inner iframe and extension host, capped at 50 events to prevent log flooding. It extracts origin, channel, target, and payload structure.\n2. A delayed check (3s) for `__CEL_LATEST_SET_HTML_INFO__` and `__CEL_LAST_SET_HTML_INFO__` globals to report `setHtml` operations via `SKY_SET_HTML` and `SKY_FIRST_SET_HTML` events.\n\nThese additions enhance observability for debugging UI bridging issues between the Sky component layer and the extension host, complementing existing DOM state and React hook diagnostics.",
			"SHA": "d82670e97566c7c52afc693f1a485b6e89e3f032"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:36:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				738,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add runtime DOM state and React hook diagnostics\n\nInject comprehensive runtime diagnostics into the webview content pipeline to aid debugging of rendering issues and API availability in custom environments. The injected script now performs periodic DOM state checks (every 500ms) to monitor the presence and children of the root element, logs React internal hook status (renderer count), captures a full DOM snapshot at 5s, verifies `acquireVsCodeApi` availability, and dumps the initial body structure.\n\nThese diagnostics are scoped to the first 30 seconds of the session and provide detailed telemetry on the webview's lifecycle, ensuring robust observability for the `RuntimeDiagnosticsInner` transform plugin.",
			"SHA": "6fc80a51d44e5cb0cdc23387a481beb61e170e1c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:34:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				738,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Standardize escaped quotes in webview logging diagnostics\n\nCorrect the escaping of quote characters within the injected `DEBUG_WV` logging call in `Source/Plugin/Transform/Inject/Webview/Debug/Logging.ts`. Replace double-escaped quotes (`\\\"`) with single-escaped quotes (`\"`) for the `id=\"root\"` and `type=\"module\"` string checks.\n\nThis ensures the generated JavaScript string literals are syntactically correct and the runtime diagnostics correctly identify the presence of the React root element and module scripts during webview content processing.",
			"SHA": "209fb282cd419882fa267cb175e539a004ef0421"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:32:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				738,
				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "7a8ec28a6be25fda890be4746ce2c96bd62e0d13"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:32:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				738,
				7
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add `DisableUIFixes` toggle and enhance webview logging\n\nIntroduce the `DisableUIFixes` environment variable to conditionally skip the `InjectMacTitlebarOffsetCSS` and `InjectPartZIndexCSS` transforms during the VS Code bundling pipeline. This provides a toggle for troubleshooting specific CSS injection conflicts in custom WKWebView/Tauri environments. The `InjectWebViewPolyfills` transform remains mandatory (always-on) to prevent module-eval crashes.\n\nAdditionally, extend the `Inject/Webview/Debug/Logging` transform to target the primary asynchronous content handler in addition to the unload monitor. Add runtime diagnostics that log the processed HTML length, root element presence, and module script inclusion immediately after `toContentHtml` execution. Update source files (`Source/Apply/Pipeline.ts`, `Source/Plugin/Index.ts`) and regenerate compiled outputs (`Configuration/Apply/Pipeline.js`, `Configuration/Plugin/Index.js`) to reflect these changes.\n\nImpact: Enables granular control over UI fix injection and significantly improves observability of extension webview content rendering pipelines.",
			"SHA": "9bc02ab78a8e93bc322e94bd585845e86f7515cc"
		}
	],
